# Variáveis de ambiente
# Everything, then one exception. The Next default listed `.env` and
# `.env*.local` and let `.env.production` through — which is precisely the file
# a production connection string ends up in. An allowlist of one is safer than
# a denylist somebody has to remember to extend.
.env*
!.env.example

# The dev email transport writes the last magic link here, which is a working
# credential. .next/ is ignored above; this says why it has to stay that way.
.next/last-email-link

